//! # superba-catalog
//!
//! The Codex settings catalog: what `config.toml` keys and `[features]` a given Codex
//! version understands, with their official upstream documentation, stages and
//! defaults, plus the human-curated layers on top.
//!
//! Layers (all under the repository's `catalog/` directory):
//!
//! - `dist/codex-<version>.json` ([`format::VersionCatalog`]): generated by
//!   `superba-catalog-gen` from an `openai/codex` release tag; upstream data only.
//! - `dist/index.json` + `dist/index.json.sig` ([`format::Index`]): SHA-256 manifest
//!   of every file, signed with ed25519 ([`integrity`]).
//! - `curation.toml` ([`curation::Curation`]): hand-made categories, platform hints
//!   and the "Common" list.
//! - `feeds/` ([`feeds`]): signed model list, prices, Codex and app versions.
//! - `overlay/*.toml` ([`overlay`]): official English text copied by the generator and
//!   Chinese names and explanations written per entry from the codex source.
//!
//! - `claude/` ([`claude`]): the Claude Code `settings.json` catalog (user bug 79).
//!
//! The whole tree is compiled in as the built-in snapshot ([`CatalogStore::builtin`]).
//! [`SnapshotSource`] implements [`superba_core::CatalogSource`] for the settings
//! engine (`SnapshotSource::builtin()`, or `SnapshotSource::new(load(..)?.store, os)`).
//! Remote updates ([`remote`]) exist but are **disabled by default**.
//!
//! Version lookup ([`CatalogStore::for_version`]) uses the exact version when listed,
//! else the nearest older one, and says so ([`VersionMatch::notice`]): Codex alphas
//! are cut on release branches and differ from their release, so
//! `CodexVersion::meets` must not be used for catalog lookups.

